From 3d38c93c73ba1d9ea37995cd2cd11c400258e8d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Assistant VIP BIKE <assistant@vip-bike.local>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:12:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(leads): stop operator rentals collapsing + collect client
 phone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of 45/57 rental_contract_artifacts having renter_phone = NULL:
/doc-manual's client_phone step is optional and the operator skipped it every
time, so the phone is genuinely absent from the DB (not lost mid-flow). Worse,
that keyed the lead by the operator's telegram id, collapsing ALL of one
operator's renters into a single franchize_intents row — only one renter was
ever visible on the leads page.

Changes:
- leads.ts: add nameIdentityKey() (normalized). Operator-created artifacts and
  rentals with no phone now key by normalized renter name instead of the
  operator/owner chat id, so each renter is a distinct, visible lead. Rentals
  merge into the matching artifact lead by name. Fixes the raw-name fallback
  that produced duplicates ("...Кириллович." vs "...Кириллович").
- leads-query.mjs: mirror leads.ts identity resolution exactly (skill now shows
  the same leads as the web page). Also fixes a pre-existing broken template
  literal (lines ~1156-1169) that embedded a fetch() inside a console.log(``)
  and made the entire skill fail to parse.
- doc-manual.ts: auto-suggest recent web callback (contact_click) phones in the
  client_phone step so the operator links the contract in one tap instead of
  skipping — the main cause of NULL phones going forward.
- vip-bike-ops/SKILL.md: document the lead identity resolution order.

Backfill migration (recover the few phones that exist in users) ships separately
as 20260722130000_backfill_renter_phone_from_users.sql. Most NULL phones cannot
be recovered — they were never collected.

Co-Authored-By: Assistant VIP BIKE <assistant@vip-bike.local>
